A Generalized Stein Lemma for Quantum Channels in Lean
Associated paper: Minbo Gao, Zhengfeng Ji, Chenghua Liu,
https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30762v1.

The project reuses a selected source closure of the earlier quantum-channel
Stein formalization in vendor/first-paper, associated with
https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.27196v1. Its recorded source checkpoint is
7f67d3ea4e6f2edd595f9c1f356da2fcc9124c4d.

Further dependencies are distributed under Apache-2.0:
- Hayata-Yamasaki-Group/lean-quantum, revision
  bf1c4f6aaec84948f1a1c76c0728432813404a0f.
- leanprover-community/physlib, revision
  f6e446ca99fd83b3a60743a61900cb2acb98f531, with compatibility adaptations
  and state-Stein bridge proofs. Reused Physlib proofs retain Alex Meiburg's
  copyright/author headers.

Dependency licenses, notices, and source-integrity manifests are retained
within their respective vendor directories. The earlier library's
SimultaneousDiagonalization and TraceNorm modules adapt Physlib arguments
and retain their original copyright headers.

See docs/dependencies.md for the exact release boundary. Attribution does
not imply endorsement by the upstream authors. The paper itself is not
included and remains under its original arXiv license.
